# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* sanity
# Sanity check that we are running the correct game and that the
# walkthrough commands are valid. (This test should succeed in both
# r88 and r200.)
#
{vital} ZORK I: The Great Underground Empire
West of House
>{include} _go_to_end
Your score is 350

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-48
# When destroying the painting, its value should be set to 0. So if you
# destroy it before picking it up, you won't get any points for it.
#
>{include} _go_to_gallery
> score
Your score is 40
> destroy painting with sword
> get painting
> score
Your score is 40

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-50-open
# You should not be able to open the bird's nest.
#
>{include} _go_to_nest
> open nest
You can't do that.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-50-close
# You should not be able to close the bird's nest.
#
>{include} _go_to_nest
> close nest
You can't do that.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-57
# TAKE ALL while you're in the boat should refuse to take the boat but
# continue taking other objects, like the label.
#
>{include} _go_to_boat
> take all
tan label: Taken.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-62
# Dropping the bird's nest from up in the tree should cause it to fall
# to the ground below.
#
>{include} _go_to_nest
> get nest
> drop nest
> d
There is a bird's nest here.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-69
# Opening the grate from above should not say that there are trees
# above you.
#
>{include} _go_to_unlocked_clearing
> close grate
> open grate
!trees above you

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-70-lock-while-open
# Locking the grate should only work if the grate is closed.
#
>{include} _go_to_grating_room
> unlock grate
> open grate
> lock grate
The grate is open.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-70-lock-while-locked
# Locking the grate should only work if the grate is unlocked.
#
>{include} _go_to_grating_room
> lock grate
already locked

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-70-unlock-while-open
# Unlocking the grate should only work if the grate is closed.
#
>{include} _go_to_grating_room
> unlock grate
> open grate
> unlock grate
already open

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-70-unlock-while-unlocked
# Unlocking the grate should only work if the grate is unlocked.
#
>{include} _go_to_grating_room
> unlock grate
> unlock grate
already unlocked

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-70-lock-with-anything
# Locking the grate should only work with the key, not other objects.
#
>{include} _go_to_grating_room
> unlock grate
> lock grate with chalice
Can you lock a grating with
> lock grate with egg
Can you lock a grating with
> lock grate with canary
Can you lock a grating with
> lock grate with bag
Can you lock a grating with
> lock grate with lantern
Can you lock a grating with

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-71
# Items visible on the ground below should be described when up in tree.
#
> open mailbox
> take leaflet
> n
> n
> drop leaflet
> u
On the ground below you can see: a leaflet.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-73
# When you kill the thief in his lair, only declare the chalice safe to
# take if the chalice is still there
#
>{include} _go_to_treasure_room
> kill thief
> kill thief
> kill thief
> kill thief
> take chalice
Taken.
> kill thief
!chalice is now safe to take

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* nathan-75
# Putting objects in the grate from the Grating Room should not say they
# go "into the darkness below".
#
>{include} _go_to_grating_room
> unlock grate
> open grate
> put egg in grate
!into the darkness below

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* tree-climb-down
# CLIMB DOWN from up in the tree should just work without printing
# "(down the tree)".
>{include} _go_to_nest
> climb down
!down the tree

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* troll-unconscious-silent
# The troll should not make any sound when he's unconscious.
#
>{include} _go_to_troll_room
> kill troll
> kill troll
> listen to troll
The troll makes no sound.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* dome-room-pour
# Issuing nonsensical commands like POUR FOO FROM ROPE in the Dome Room
# should not drop the rope down to the room below.
#
>{include} _go_to_dome_room
> pour painting from rope
!rope

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* dome-room-jump
# Jumping in the Dome Room should kill you with a specific message.
#
>{include} _go_to_dome_room
> jump
I'm afraid that the leap you attempted has done you in.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* dome-room-jump-over
# Jumping over the railing in the Dome Room should kill you.
#
>{include} _go_to_dome_room
> jump over railing
You have died

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* dome-room-climb-down
# CLIMB DOWN from the Dome Room should work, as long as the rope is in
# place.
#
>{include} _go_to_dome_room
> tie rope to railing
> climb down
Torch Room

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* maze-taunt
# The thief should pick up objects dropped in the maze and taunt you
# about it.
#
>{include} _go_to_maze
> s. e. u
> get bag and key
> sw. e. s
I wonder what this fine rusty knife is doing here.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* cyclops-room-throw
# Throwing something at the sleeping cyclops should wake him up.
#
>{include} _go_to_cyclops_room
> throw knife at cyclops
woke him up

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* buoy-funny
# You should notice something funny when you pick up the buoy.
#
>{include} _go_to_boat
> launch
> get buoy
You notice something funny

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* burn-leaves
# Burning the leaves while they are on the ground should not kill you.
#
>{include} _go_to_dam_lobby
> s. w. sw. sw. w. s. u
> e. e. n. n. n. d
> light match
> burn leaves
!You have died

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* burn-leaves-in-boat
# Burning the leaves while they are in a container you are not carrying
# (e.g. the inflated boat) should not kill you.
#
>{include} _go_to_boat
> get out of boat
> drop all but lantern
> n. w. w. w. w. w. s. u
> e. e. n. n. n. d
> take leaves
> u. s. s. e. w. w
> take matchbook
> d. n. e. e. e. e. e. s
> put leaves in boat
> light match
> burn leaves
!You have died

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
* lose-light-match
# When a lit match is your only light source and it goes out, the game
# should say "It is now pitch black."
#
>{include}_go_to_end_living_room
> take matchbook
> d
> turn off lamp
> light match
> wait
It is now pitch black.
